Summary of Logical Relationships

• G1 → (G2 ; G3) [AND sequential branch]  
 – Justification: For a single item, the collection phase (G2) must be fully completed before the delivery phase (G3) begins.

• G1 → G5 [OR branch]  
 – Justification: When multiple items are required, the mission can be executed in parallel (G5) instead of sequentially. Fulfilling the parallel branch is an acceptable alternative to the sequential branch.

• G2 → {AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4, AT9} [AND]  
 – Justification: All collection tasks must be executed in sequence to ensure the resource is properly retrieved.

• G3 → {AT5, AT6, AT7, AT8, AT10, AT11} [AND]  
 – Justification: All delivery tasks (including battery monitoring and fallback) must be completed to ensure safe and complete delivery.

• G5 → {AT12, AT13, AT14, AT15, AT16, AT17, AT18} [Parallel (#)]  
 – Justification: In the parallel branch, each resource’s collection and delivery tasks are executed concurrently, reducing overall mission time.

